INT. MOSS THRONE ROOM OF THE WILLOW KING - DAY

A hollow inside a colossal willow. Roots coil into pillars. Glowworms hang like chandeliers. Dew drips into a stone basin.

KING ALDERMERE THE GREEN, ancient, bark-skinned, crowned with antlers, sits upon a throne of woven roots.

Before him kneel five petitioners: a fox-faced RANGER named SIORA, a hulking BADGER-SMITH named BRONWYN, twin sprites TANSY and BRAMBLE with dragonfly wings, and a hooded MONK named IVO.

ALDERMERE
Speak, children of the glade.

SIORA
Majesty, the river runs thin.

BRONWYN
The fish are gone.

TANSY
Say it softly, sister.

BRAMBLE ^
Say it softly, sister.

They look at each other, annoyed, then back at the king.

IVO
(hood low)
We have come about the stag.

ALDERMERE
The stag is dead.

SIORA
The stag is walking.

Silence. Glowworms flicker. A drop falls in the basin.

ALDERMERE
Show me.

Ivo lowers his hood. From his own skull rise pale antlers dripping moss, and his eyes are dead lamps.

The king rises.
